# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classically simulating circuits with OBP for the latest version of Operator backpropagation (OBP)"
msgstr "Simulasi klasik circuit dengan OBP untuk versi terbaru Operator backpropagation (OBP)"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classically simulating circuits with OBP"
msgstr "Simulasi klasik circuit dengan OBP"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/simulating-circuits-with-obp.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this guide, you will learn how to classically simulate `QuantumCircuit` instances to estimate expectation values entirely through the means of OBP.\n"
msgstr "Di panduan ini, kamu akan belajar cara mensimulasikan instance `QuantumCircuit` secara klasik untuk memperkirakan nilai ekspektasi sepenuhnya lewat OBP.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since OBP will take an observable and backpropagate it through a given circuit, the \"simulation\" of a circuit amounts to computing the expectation value of the target observable with respect to this circuit.\n"
"As you will see later, the `qiskit-addon-obp` package is even capable of handling simple noise models, allowing you to compute noisy expectation values, too!\n"
msgstr ""
"Karena OBP mengambil sebuah observable dan melakukan backpropagation melewati circuit tertentu, \"simulasi\" sebuah circuit sama dengan menghitung nilai ekspektasi observable target terhadap circuit tersebut.\n"
"Seperti yang akan kamu lihat nanti, paket `qiskit-addon-obp` bahkan bisa menangani model noise sederhana, sehingga kamu bisa menghitung nilai ekspektasi yang noisy juga!\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Constructing an example circuit {#constructing-an-example-circuit}"
msgstr "Membangun contoh circuit {#constructing-an-example-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the purposes of this guide, we will use the same example circuit as in the [Pauli term truncation guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms):\n"
msgstr "Untuk keperluan panduan ini, kita akan memakai contoh circuit yang sama seperti di [panduan pemangkasan suku Pauli](/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, the above is purely the circuit describing the time evolution under a chosen Hamiltonian.\n"
"We also need an initial state to start from, with respect to which we compute the expectation values of our observable.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tapi, yang di atas itu murni circuit yang menggambarkan evolusi waktu di bawah Hamiltonian pilihan.\n"
"Kita juga butuh state awal sebagai titik mulai, yang terhadapnya kita menghitung nilai ekspektasi observable kita.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Of course, we could choose the all-zero (or vacuum) state as our initial state, but to show how one would insert their own initial state, we choose a different one below.\n"
msgstr "Tentu saja kita bisa memilih state all-zero (atau vakum) sebagai state awal, tapi untuk menunjukkan cara memasukkan state awal sendiri, di bawah ini kita pilih yang lain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One possibility, would be to prepend the initial state to our time-evolution circuit above: `circuit.compose(initial_state, front=True)`.\n"
"But since we have already sliced our `circuit`, it is easier to simply insert the initial state as the first slice, which we do below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Salah satu caranya adalah menaruh state awal di depan circuit evolusi waktu di atas: `circuit.compose(initial_state, front=True)`.\n"
"Tapi karena kita sudah mengiris `circuit` kita, lebih mudah memasukkan state awal sebagai slice pertama, yang kita lakukan di bawah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this way, we can simply replace the first slice with another initial state, if we want to exchange that in the future, without having to recompute our slices.\n"
msgstr "Dengan cara ini, kita bisa dengan mudah mengganti slice pertama dengan state awal lain kalau nanti ingin menukarnya, tanpa harus menghitung ulang slice kita.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
