# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulating a noiseless expectation value {#simulating-a-noiseless-expectation-value}"
msgstr "Mensimulasikan nilai ekspektasi tanpa noise {#simulating-a-noiseless-expectation-value}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As our target observable, we choose the `ZZ` observable on the central qubits:\n"
msgstr "Sebagai observable target, kita pilih observable `ZZ` pada qubit di tengah:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point, we are already set to classically simulate the expectation value using OBP.\n"
"To do so, we simply provide the _all_ the slices to the `backpropagate` method, like so:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sampai di sini, kita sudah siap mensimulasikan nilai ekspektasi secara klasik dengan OBP.\n"
"Caranya, kita cukup memberikan _semua_ slice ke metode `backpropagate`, seperti ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We have now backpropagated our target observable `obs` through the _entire_ circuit (**including** the `initial_state` which we placed on `slices[0]`) resulting in a new `SparsePauliOp` whose expectation value we obtain by projecting it on the _vacuum state_ (`|00...00>`).\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita sudah melakukan backpropagation pada observable target `obs` melewati _seluruh_ circuit (**termasuk** `initial_state` yang kita taruh di `slices[0]`), menghasilkan `SparsePauliOp` baru yang nilai ekspektasinya kita dapatkan dengan memproyeksikannya ke _state vakum_ (`|00...00>`).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This can be achieved in a straight forward manner by summing up the coefficients of all Pauli terms defined in the computational basis:\n"
msgstr "Ini bisa dicapai dengan cara yang lugas, yaitu menjumlahkan koefisien semua suku Pauli yang didefinisikan dalam basis komputasional:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a sanity check (and to prove that this works) we can compare our result against Qiskit's `Statevector`:\n"
msgstr "Sebagai sanity check (dan untuk membuktikan bahwa ini berhasil), kita bisa membandingkan hasil kita dengan `Statevector` milik Qiskit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some notes on performance {#some-notes-on-performance}"
msgstr "Beberapa catatan soal performa {#some-notes-on-performance}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The computational efficiency of the `backpropagate` call above will heavily depend on many things, including:\n"
"- the structure of the `circuit`\n"
"- the method of slicing the circuit\n"
"- the target observable\n"
"- the truncation parameters\n"
msgstr ""
"Efisiensi komputasi dari pemanggilan `backpropagate` di atas sangat bergantung pada banyak hal, antara lain:\n"
"- struktur `circuit`\n"
"- metode pengirisan circuit\n"
"- observable target\n"
"- parameter pemangkasan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since the `backpropagate` method simplifies the observable after every _slice_ has been applied, the number of gates in a slice can dramatically influence the computational burden.\n"
"The most aggressive strategy in terms of operator simplification can be achieved by slicing your circuit into slices of individual gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Karena metode `backpropagate` menyederhanakan observable setiap kali satu _slice_ selesai diterapkan, jumlah gate dalam sebuah slice bisa sangat memengaruhi beban komputasi.\n"
"Strategi penyederhanaan operator yang paling agresif bisa dicapai dengan mengiris circuit kamu menjadi slice berisi gate tunggal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Additionally, you can leverage all of the truncation mechanism built into the `backpropagate` method.\n"
"We did not do so above, effectively resulting in an exact expectation value, but you can learn how to in the [Pauli term truncation guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms).\n"
msgstr ""
"Selain itu, kamu bisa memanfaatkan semua mekanisme pemangkasan yang tertanam di metode `backpropagate`.\n"
"Di atas kita tidak melakukannya, sehingga hasilnya adalah nilai ekspektasi yang tepat, tapi kamu bisa belajar caranya di [panduan pemangkasan suku Pauli](/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulating a noisy expectation value {#simulating-a-noisy-expectation-value}"
msgstr "Mensimulasikan nilai ekspektasi yang noisy {#simulating-a-noisy-expectation-value}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `qiskit-addon-obp` package also supports handling of noise models in the form of `PauliLindbladError`s.\n"
"This is especially useful when you have characterized the noise model of the 2-qubit layers in your circuit, for example using the [`NoiseLearner`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/noise-learner-noise-learner).\n"
msgstr ""
"Paket `qiskit-addon-obp` juga mendukung penanganan model noise dalam bentuk `PauliLindbladError`.\n"
"Ini sangat berguna kalau kamu sudah mengkarakterisasi model noise dari layer 2-qubit di circuit kamu, misalnya memakai [`NoiseLearner`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/noise-learner-noise-learner).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this section, you will see how you can use the `LayerError` objects returned by the `NoiseLearner` to compute noisy expectation values using OBP.\n"
msgstr "Di bagian ini, kamu akan melihat cara memakai objek `LayerError` yang dikembalikan oleh `NoiseLearner` untuk menghitung nilai ekspektasi yang noisy dengan OBP.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Obtaining a noise model {#obtaining-a-noise-model}"
msgstr "Mendapatkan model noise {#obtaining-a-noise-model}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Normally, you would execute the `NoiseLearner` to obtain a noise model of your specific circuit.\n"
"To avoid complexity (and randomness) in this tutorial, we will refrain from doing so, and instead hard-code some noise model for our circuit below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Biasanya, kamu akan menjalankan `NoiseLearner` untuk mendapatkan model noise dari circuit spesifik kamu.\n"
"Untuk menghindari kerumitan (dan keacakan) di tutorial ini, kita tidak melakukannya, dan sebagai gantinya kita menulis langsung (hard-code) sebuah model noise untuk circuit kita di bawah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, we make sure that the structure of our data matches that of the [`NoiseLearnerResult`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/results-noise-learner-result).\n"
"In its current (non-transpiled) form, our circuit contains 4 unique layers of 2-qubit gates:\n"
"- `slices[1]`: which has `Rxx` gates acting on all odd pairs of qubits\n"
"- `slices[2]`: which has `Rxx` gates acting on all even pairs of qubits\n"
"- `slices[3]`: which has `Ryy` gates acting on all odd pairs of qubits\n"
"- `slices[4]`: which has `Ryy` gates acting on all even pairs of qubits\n"
msgstr ""
"Meski begitu, kita pastikan struktur data kita cocok dengan [`NoiseLearnerResult`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/results-noise-learner-result).\n"
"Dalam bentuknya saat ini (belum di-transpile), circuit kita berisi 4 layer unik gate 2-qubit:\n"
"- `slices[1]`: berisi gate `Rxx` yang bekerja pada semua pasangan qubit ganjil\n"
"- `slices[2]`: berisi gate `Rxx` yang bekerja pada semua pasangan qubit genap\n"
"- `slices[3]`: berisi gate `Ryy` yang bekerja pada semua pasangan qubit ganjil\n"
"- `slices[4]`: berisi gate `Ryy` yang bekerja pada semua pasangan qubit genap\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the cell below, we manually construct 4 `LayerError` instances for each one of these layers with some randomized error rates.\n"
msgstr "Di cell di bawah, kita membuat secara manual 4 instance `LayerError` untuk masing-masing layer ini dengan error rate acak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you would have used the `NoiseLearner` to identify the unique 2-qubit gate layers of your circuit and characterize their noise, you would obtain a `NoiseLearnerResult` object.\n"
"This result would contain a list of `LayerError` objects, just like the ones we have manually constructed above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kalau kamu memakai `NoiseLearner` untuk mengidentifikasi layer gate 2-qubit yang unik dari circuit kamu dan mengkarakterisasi noise-nya, kamu akan mendapatkan objek `NoiseLearnerResult`.\n"
"Hasil ini akan berisi daftar objek `LayerError`, seperti yang sudah kita buat secara manual di atas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For each unique 2-qubit layer, the `LayerError` contains:\n"
"- the `QuantumCircuit` representing that 2-qubit gate layer\n"
"- the qubit indices which this circuit is acting upon\n"
"- the `PauliLindbladError` which represents the characterized noise model of this layer\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk setiap layer 2-qubit yang unik, `LayerError` berisi:\n"
"- `QuantumCircuit` yang merepresentasikan layer gate 2-qubit tersebut\n"
"- indeks qubit tempat circuit ini bekerja\n"
"- `PauliLindbladError` yang merepresentasikan model noise hasil karakterisasi dari layer ini\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `PauliLindbladError` will contain two objects:\n"
"- the list of Pauli errors that have been characterized\n"
"- the error rates corresponding to each one of those Pauli errors\n"
msgstr ""
"`PauliLindbladError` akan berisi dua objek:\n"
"- daftar error Pauli yang sudah dikarakterisasi\n"
"- error rate yang sesuai dengan masing-masing error Pauli tersebut\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normally, the list of Pauli errors will be sparse. More specifically, it will contain the single-qubit Pauli errors on all qubits that have gates acting upon them as well as the two-qubit Pauli errors on all those qubits that are connected.\n"
msgstr "Biasanya, daftar error Pauli bersifat sparse. Lebih spesifik, daftar ini berisi error Pauli satu-qubit pada semua qubit yang dikenai gate, serta error Pauli dua-qubit pada semua qubit yang saling terhubung.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inserting the noisy layers into our circuit {#inserting-the-noisy-layers-into-our-circuit}"
msgstr "Menyisipkan layer noisy ke circuit kita {#inserting-the-noisy-layers-into-our-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the previous section, we have specifically constructed one `LayerError` for each of our known unique 2-qubit gate layers.\n"
"This means, we know which `LayerError` matches a specific one of our slices exactly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di bagian sebelumnya, kita secara khusus membuat satu `LayerError` untuk setiap layer gate 2-qubit unik yang kita ketahui.\n"
"Artinya, kita tahu persis `LayerError` mana yang cocok dengan salah satu slice kita.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Normally, when using the `LayerError`, you will need to figure out what the unique 2-qubit gate layer is, and where it occurs inside of your circuit.\n"
"You will then need to adjust your `circuit` and/or `slices` to insert the `LayerError` accordingly.\n"
"How to do this in the general case, is beyond the scope of this how-to guide.\n"
"**TODO: link to external documentation, once it exists!**\n"
"Here, our life is simpler because we know which slice a `LayerError` corresponds to.\n"
"Therefore, it is now just a matter of inserting new slices to represent the noise.\n"
msgstr ""
"Biasanya, saat memakai `LayerError`, kamu perlu mencari tahu apa layer gate 2-qubit yang unik itu, dan di mana letaknya di dalam circuit kamu.\n"
"Lalu kamu perlu menyesuaikan `circuit` dan/atau `slices` kamu untuk menyisipkan `LayerError` tersebut.\n"
"Cara melakukannya untuk kasus umum berada di luar cakupan panduan how-to ini.\n"
"**TODO: link to external documentation, once it exists!**\n"
"Di sini, urusannya lebih sederhana karena kita tahu slice mana yang sesuai dengan sebuah `LayerError`.\n"
"Jadi, tinggal menyisipkan slice baru untuk merepresentasikan noise.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note, that we must wrap each `PauliLindbladError` from `LayerError.error` in a `PauliLindbladErrorInstruction` for it to be a valid `QuantumCircuit` instruction.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bahwa kita harus membungkus setiap `PauliLindbladError` dari `LayerError.error` dalam `PauliLindbladErrorInstruction` agar menjadi instruksi `QuantumCircuit` yang valid.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can check our work and draw the circuit below:\n"
msgstr "Kita bisa memeriksa hasil kerja kita dan menggambar circuit di bawah:\n"

